# Line endings are normalised to LF inside the repository whatever machine
# commits, while the working copy stays native. Without this, committing from
# Windows can put CRLF in the repo, and a CRLF `gradlew` fails on Linux and
# macOS with a "bad interpreter" error that gives no hint what is wrong.
* text=auto

# The Gradle wrapper script is read by sh, so it is LF everywhere, including
# in a Windows checkout. Its .bat twin is the opposite.
gradlew text eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never line-ending-mangle these.
*.jar binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.apk binary
*.aab binary
*.jks binary
*.keystore binary
